# (1.5.0, Decisions 7) What a cue shows, what it says, and its mutes at a stop:
# 1. a cue shows the card its key or knob would ("CHORD THROW", "KICK muted", "SOLO", "FREEZE held", "WAIL", "LOCK"),
#    a grid effect's, dub hold's and a knob's name in the header, the DJ filter's ring; the screen reader says none of
#    it (said_none), and still says what the player does (a key tapped: "CHORD OFF");
# 2. the mutes and solos the cues changed are put back as they were when the music stops (PLAY): those you tapped since
#    are yours and stay (the hats tapped twice), a part you muted that a cue unmuted is muted again (the noise); a Mix
#    carries a cue's mute into the next piece, and the stop after it undoes it.
# (build: DUB1_CUES=1) the cues played: run on build/host/amb_host_cues (the release plays none: nocues.amb)
listen
wait 1500
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
expect piece 0
# Basic's cues, each a bar from PLAY (part b)
cue 0 b 1 0 move 0 0 8
cue 0 b 2 0 mute 3 1 0
cue 0 b 3 0 solo 2 1 0
cue 0 b 4 0 fx 6 0 8
cue 0 b 5 0 fx 10 0 8
cue 0 b 6 0 siren 0 0 0
cue 0 b 7 0 macro 0 -20 16
cue 0 b 8 0 knob 15 60 16
cue 0 b 9 0 lock 0 1 0
cue 0 b 10 0 hold 0 1 0
cue 0 b 11 0 hold 0 0 0
cue 0 b 12 0 lock 0 0 0
cue 0 b 13 0 mute 4 1 0
cue 0 b 14 0 mute 5 0 0
cue 0 b 15 0 move 1 0 8
cue 0 b 16 0 outro 0 0 0
cuesave
expect slotcues0 16
tap SEL
wait 300
expect view 17
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect playing 1
expect cuelive 1
# the player's own: the chord and the noise muted by hand, said as ever
tapkey w0
wait 100
said CHORD OFF
expect mutes 1
tapkey w5
wait 100
said NOISE OFF
expect mutes 33
wait 1200
bar 1
wait 50
expect cuemoves 1
cardis CHORD THROW
bar 2
wait 50
expect mutes 41
cardis KICK
bar 3
wait 50
expect solo 4
cardis SOLO
bar 4
wait 50
expect cuefx 64
cardis -
msgis Wah
bar 5
wait 50
expect cuefx 1024
cardis FREEZE
bar 6
wait 50
cardis WAIL
bar 7
wait 50
expect fltring 1
bar 8
wait 50
msgis MOTION
bar 9
wait 50
expect lock 1
cardis LOCK
bar 10
wait 50
expect frozen 1
msgis DUB HOLD
bar 11
wait 50
expect frozen 0
bar 12
wait 50
expect lock 0
bar 13
wait 50
expect mutes 57
cardis HATS
bar 14
wait 50
expect mutes 25
cardis NOISE
bar 15
wait 50
cardis OPEN
# none of it said
said_none THROW
said_none KICK
said_none SOLO
said_none Wah
said_none FREEZE
said_none WAIL
said_none FILTER
said_none MOTION
said_none LOCK
said_none DUB HOLD
said_none HATS
said_none NOISE
said_none OPEN
# the hats, a cue's mute, tapped off and on again by hand: yours now
tapkey w4
wait 100
said HATS ON
tapkey w4
wait 100
said HATS OFF
expect mutes 25
bar 16
wait 50
cardis OUTRO
said_none OUTRO
# stopped: the kick (a cue's) on again, the bass's solo off, the noise (yours, a cue unmuted it) muted again; the chord
# and the hats (yours) kept
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
expect mutes 49
expect solo 0
# the same with a Mix: Basic's outro mutes the hats; carried into Chamber's downbeat; undone at the stop after it
cueclear 0
cue 0 o 2 0 mute 4 1 0
cuesave
expect slotcues0 1
tapkey w0
tapkey w4
tapkey w5
wait 100
expect mutes 0
tap GLO
wait 200
tap GLO
wait 400
expect view 28
spin K1 2
wait 300
spin K2 2
wait 300
expect par158 2
expect trans 2
expect cuesoff 0
# two short songs: Basic (no intro, Main 32 bars, Outro 16), then Chamber
turn PRESET 1
wait 600
tap HOME
wait 200
tap HOME
wait 300
spin K1 -2
spin K2 -16
spin K3 -2
wait 300
turn PRESET -1
wait 600
spin K1 -4
spin K2 -16
spin K3 -2
wait 300
expect piece 0
tap SEL
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect playing 1
bar 34
wait 50
expect mutes 16
cardis HATS
bar 47
wait 1500
expect piece 1
wait 1000
expect trcue 0
expect song 1
expect mutes 16
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
expect mutes 0
expect solo 0
# Transition LP: a Set's own rest between two songs isn't a stop (the next comes by itself): the hats stay muted into
# Chamber, undone at the stop after
tap SEL
wait 300
tap GLO
wait 200
tap GLO
wait 400
expect view 28
spin K2 -4
wait 300
expect trans 0
turn PRESET -1
wait 600
expect piece 0
tap SEL
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 100
expect playing 1
bar 34
wait 50
expect mutes 16
bar 48
wait 3000
expect playing 0
expect mutes 16
wait 6000
expect playing 1
expect piece 1
expect mutes 16
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
expect mutes 0
